{"parentUuid":"b40bf04b-9472-4ba6-a1b8-e0ce47bb016e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a241150d7be611784","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GXAaPDL4BYsNGhyWckucxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Psw7FwwzbEUtNqVZvVBcPx","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"GPU MIP branch and bound 2025 viable solver consumer GPU"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8782,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8782},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8782,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozbfEftHNVwrMUXpMcR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e573e10c-02f6-48d6-827a-2c305921fd6c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:50.995Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2d40a00b-21c0-451e-97f2-f4842358bab0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013qrYdX4covkLz35rjkXK8N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cuPDLPx 2025 GPU LP solver benchmark NVIDIA release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx: A GPU-Accelerated First-Order LP Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: Enhanced GPU LP Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2507.14051\"},{\"title\":\"How to Get Started with NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.akamai.com/blog/cloud/2025/oct/how-to-get-started-nvidia-cuopt\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.14051\"},{\"title\":\"Presolving for GPU-Accelerated First-Order LP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.23951\"},{\"title\":\"Solve Linear Programs Using the GPU-Accelerated Barrier Method in NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/solve-linear-programs-using-the-gpu-accelerated-barrier-method-in-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP+: GPU-Based LP Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/cupdlp\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2025arXiv250714051L/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started with NVIDIA CuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://atalaykutlay.com/getting-started-with-cuopt.html\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.connectedpapers.com/main/fb2c8fd720e57fe075364500b17ad55f3560be34\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cuPDLPx:\n\n## cuPDLPx: A 2025 GPU-Based LP Solver\n\ncuPDLPx is a GPU-accelerated linear programming solver based on a restarted Halpern PDHG method specifically tailored for GPU architectures. It incorporates a new restart criterion and a PID-controlled primal weight update, with these improvements carefully tailored for GPU architectures and delivering substantial computational gains.\n\n### Benchmark Performance\n\nThe solver demonstrates impressive performance improvements:\n\n- cuPDLPx achieves 2.5x-5x speedups on MIPLIB LP relaxations and 3x-6.8x on Mittelmann's benchmark set, with particularly strong improvements in high-accuracy and presolve-enabled settings.\n\n### Technical Details\n\nThe benchmarking experiments used an NVIDIA H100-SXM-80GB GPU with CUDA 12.4. The solver is publicly available at https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx.\n\nThe cupdlpx Python package supports building and solving LPs directly with NumPy and SciPy.\n\n### Publication\n\nA detailed research paper titled \"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\" was published on arXiv in 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3e400a20-c2be-4db3-8efa-57840eaa5f9d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:54.927Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2d40a00b-21c0-451e-97f2-f4842358bab0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b40bf04b-9472-4ba6-a1b8-e0ce47bb016e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SrSHjcNsLFG9ub9XSEbVhv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NVIDIA cuOpt 2026 open source MIP LP solver release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - NVIDIA/cuopt: GPU accelerated decision optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Decision Optimization Using Open Source NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-decision-optimization-using-open-source-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"cuOpt | Decision Optimization | NVIDIA\",\"url\":\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Rose cuOpt - SimpleRose\",\"url\":\"https://simplerose.com/rosecuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA cuOpt Solver Cracks Four Previously Unsolved Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://bitcoinethereumnews.com/tech/nvidia-cuopt-solver-cracks-four-previously-unsolved-optimization-problems/\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA AI Developer on X: \\\"History made 🏆 NVIDIA cuOpt just won the 2026 LPFeas Hans Mittelmann leaderboard, becoming the world’s fastest open-source LP solver. The GPU-accelerated chain reaction in decision optimization is here, with three out of the four LP solvers now GPU-accelerated. Get started: https://t.co/f1UHHpxoD7\\\" / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/NVIDIAAIDev/status/2011951538449559695\"},{\"title\":\"News – COIN-OR: Computational Infrastructure for Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.coin-or.org/news/\"},{\"title\":\"History made 🏆 NVIDIA cuOpt just won the 2026 LPFeas ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.facebook.com/NVIDIAAI/posts/history-made-nvidia-cuopt-just-won-the-2026-lpfeas-hans-mittelmann-leaderboard-b/1317687737062171/\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA's Open Source cuOpt Revolutionizes Decision Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://bitcoinethereumnews.com/tech/nvidias-open-source-cuopt-revolutionizes-decision-optimization/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about NVIDIA cuOpt's 2026 open-source MIP/LP solver release:\n\n## Open Source Release\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt is now available as open source under the Apache 2.0 license, and has been added to the COIN-OR repository on Github as an open source library implementing GPU-accelerated algorithms for optimization.\n\n## Capabilities\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt is a GPU-accelerated optimization engine that excels in mixed integer linear programming (MILP), linear programming (LP), quadratic programming (QP), and vehicle routing problems (VRP). It enables near real-time solutions for large-scale LPs with millions of variables and constraints, and MIPs with hundreds of thousands of variables.\n\n## 2026 Performance Achievements\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt just won the 2026 LPFeas Hans Mittelmann leaderboard, becoming the world's fastest open-source LP solver. Additionally, NVIDIA's GPU-accelerated cuOpt engine discovered solutions for four previously unsolved problems in the MIPLIB benchmark set.\n\n## Integration and Deployment\n\ncuOpt can be easily integrated into existing models built with PuLP and AMPL with minimal refactoring, and it offers multiple interfaces, including Python API, REST API, and command-line interface (CLI).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"167ddcb5-f978-4757-ae87-6c65874eb4f5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:56.197Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b40bf04b-9472-4ba6-a1b8-e0ce47bb016e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2b424cf4-5a9f-433c-b581-4819eaf4f4ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0155rprW6qjB6CdvD7oukgKq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PDLP cuPDLP-C 2026 production GPU linear programming solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cuPDLP.jl: A GPU Implementation of Restarted Primal-Dual ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2311.12180\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - COPT-Public/cuPDLP-C: Code for solving LP on GPU using first-order methods\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/COPT-Public/cuPDLP-C\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP.jl: A GPU Implementation of Restarted Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient for Linear Programming in Julia | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.2024.1069\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP+: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.14051v1\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.14051\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx: A GPU-Accelerated First-Order LP Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP.jl: A GPU Implementation of Restarted Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient for Linear Programming in Julia\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2311.12180v3\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Large Linear Programming Problems with NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-large-linear-programming-problems-with-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jinwen-yang/cuPDLP.jl: GPU-based first-order solver for linear programming.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jinwen-yang/cuPDLP.jl\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP-C: A Strengthened Implementation of cuPDLP for Linear Programming by C language\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.14832\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about PDLP and cuPDLP-C:\n\n## Overview\n\ncuPDLP.jl is a GPU implementation of restarted primal-dual hybrid gradient for solving linear programming (LP). cuPDLP-C is the C implementation of the Julia version cuPDLP.jl.\n\n## cuPDLP-C Details\n\ncuPDLP-C is an enhanced C implementation of cuPDLP, providing substantial evidence that GPUs can significantly accelerate first-order linear programming solvers. cuPDLP-C demonstrates compelling performance on classic LP benchmarks, including the LP relaxations of MIPLIB 2017 instances and Mittelmann's LP benchmark in finding primal-dual feasible points even compared to commercial IPM-based solvers like COPT.\n\n## Algorithm Foundation\n\nPDLP is a first-order method (FOM) LP solver, with the fundamental difference that the computational bottleneck of FOM is (sparse) matrix-vector multiplication, in contrast to (sparse) matrix factorization in simplex or IPMs.\n\n## GitHub Repository\n\ncuPDLP-C is code for solving LP on GPU using the first-order algorithm PDLP, and is the C implementation of the Julia version cuPDLP.jl. The source code is available at https://github.com/COPT-Public/cuPDLP-C.\n\nNote: My search results don't contain specific information about a 2026 production release or status. The most recent versions documented appear to include cuPDLPx (released in 2025) and other enhanced versions of the solver.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ec073d98-786c-4695-88d6-25d57076925c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:57.228Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b424cf4-5a9f-433c-b581-4819eaf4f4ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e573e10c-02f6-48d6-827a-2c305921fd6c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Psw7FwwzbEUtNqVZvVBcPx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GPU MIP branch and bound 2025 viable solver consumer GPU\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learn How NVIDIA cuOpt Accelerates Mixed Integer Optimization using Primal Heuristics | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/learn-how-nvidia-cuopt-accelerates-mixed-integer-optimization-using-primal-heuristics\"},{\"title\":\"Using GPUs to Solve LPs vs. MIPs: What’s the Difference? - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/using-gpus-to-solve-lps-vs-mips-whats-the-difference/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Primal Heuristics for Mixed Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=JtwE7RMyFR\"},{\"title\":\"Design Considerations for GPU-based Mixed Integer Programming on Parallel Computing Platforms | 50th International Conference on Parallel Processing Workshop\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3458744.3473366\"},{\"title\":\"Design Considerations for GPU-based Mixed Integer ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1817473\"},{\"title\":\"Part 4: Where GPUs Really Speed Up Optimization: Targeted Acceleration in Mathematical Solvers - SimpleRose\",\"url\":\"https://simplerose.com/blog/gpu-optimization-part4/\"},{\"title\":\"Using GPUs to Solve LPs vs. MIPs | Gurobi\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/blog/using-gpus-to-solve-lps-vs-mips-what-s-the-difference\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"A GPU-Aware Batched Branch and Bound Method for Solving Mixed-Binary MPC Problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395439865_A_GPU-Aware_Batched_Branch_and_Bound_Method_for_Solving_Mixed-Binary_MPC_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - NVIDIA/cuopt: GPU accelerated decision optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding GPU-based branch and bound solvers for MIP (Mixed Integer Programming) on consumer GPUs in 2025:\n\n## Current State of GPU-Based Branch and Bound\n\nAccelerating the Branch-and-Bound algorithms for MIPs using GPUs is still an active area of research. While significant progress has been made, full branch and bound implementations on consumer GPUs remain challenging.\n\n## Practical GPU Solutions for MIP\n\nRather than implementing complete branch and bound on GPUs, the industry has adopted hybrid approaches:\n\n**NVIDIA cuOpt**: For MIP, NVIDIA cuOpt uses a hybrid GPU/CPU method, running primal heuristics on the GPU and improving the dual bound on the CPU. NVIDIA® cuOpt™ is a GPU-accelerated optimization engine that excels in mixed integer linear programming (MILP), linear programming (LP), quadratic programming (QP), and vehicle routing problems (VRP).\n\n**Consumer GPU Support**: cuOpt requires an NVIDIA GPU with a Volta architecture or newer, with powerful GPUs such as the NVIDIA V100, A100, H100/H200, and the latest Blackwell series B100/B200 supported.\n\n## When GPUs Help MIP Solving\n\nCases where the majority of solve time is spent in the initial LP root relaxation may benefit from using GPUs for that step in the Branch-and-Bound framework. The incorporation of a straightforward Branch and Bound approach (excluding cutting planes) with diving threads and a subMIP-based Evolutionary Algorithm provided an even greater degree of improvement.\n\n**Bottom Line**: Full branch and bound on consumer GPUs remains primarily a research area in 2025, with practical solutions focusing on GPU-accelerated heuristics and LP relaxations within a CPU-orchestrated branch and bound framework.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f45e1efd-efe7-4fa2-b20b-a5dfa42ff072","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:03.148Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e573e10c-02f6-48d6-827a-2c305921fd6c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
