{"parentUuid":"f2d6609e-2e5e-42c9-8f89-d79808af1078","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QmBmqCpXmPVk6t4b2Lcycp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cuPDLPx RTX 4090 consumer GPU benchmark performance vs H100\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NVIDIA H100 NVL (PCIe) vs. NVIDIA RTX 4090 vs. NVIDIA RTX 4080| GPU Benchmarks for AI/ML, LLM, deep learning %current_year% | BIZON\",\"url\":\"https://bizon-tech.com/gpu-benchmarks/NVIDIA-H100-NVL-(PCIe)-vs-NVIDIA-RTX-4090-vs-NVIDIA-RTX-4080/632vs637vs638\"},{\"title\":\"RTX 4090 vs H100 PCIe | Runpod GPU Benchmarks\",\"url\":\"https://www.runpod.io/gpu-compare/rtx-4090-vs-h100-pcie\"},{\"title\":\"H100 vs RTX 4090: Making the Right Choice | TRG Datacenters\",\"url\":\"https://www.trgdatacenters.com/resource/h100-vs-4090/\"},{\"title\":\"H100 PCIe vs RTX 4090 | Runpod GPU Benchmarks\",\"url\":\"https://www.runpod.io/gpu-compare/h100-pcie-vs-rtx-4090\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 vs NVIDIA H100 SXM5 - GPU Comparison | Which Is Better\",\"url\":\"https://www.topcpu.net/en/gpu-c/geforce-rtx-4090-vs-h100-sxm5\"},{\"title\":\"So the 4090 is 38% faster (in FP32 FLOPS) than the current top server GPU (H100)... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=32914934\"},{\"title\":\"Side-by-Side Comparison - NVIDIA RTX 4090 & H100 GPUs | AIGPU Whitepaper\",\"url\":\"https://aigpu.gitbook.io/whitepaper/technology-and-development/side-by-side-comparison-nvidia-rtx-4090-and-h100-gpus\"},{\"title\":\"H100 vs A100 vs RTX 4090\",\"url\":\"https://www.gpu-mart.com/blog/h100-vs-a100-vs-rtx-4090\"},{\"title\":\"RTX 4090 vs H100 GPU Server Performance Guide | Ventus Servers\",\"url\":\"https://ventusserver.com/h100-gpu-server-performance/\"},{\"title\":\"H100 PCIe vs GeForce RTX 4090\",\"url\":\"https://technical.city/en/video/GeForce-RTX-4090-vs-H100-PCIe\"}]\n\nBased on the search results for RTX 4090 vs H100 consumer GPU benchmark performance, here are the key findings:\n\n## AI and Training Performance\n\nThe NVIDIA H100 is significantly faster than the RTX 4090 in AI and high-performance computing (HPC) tasks. For example, it can handle models with up to 65 billion parameters, while the RTX 4090 maxes out at 6 billion. More specifically, H100 achieves 248 TFLOPS FP16, 2-3x faster than RTX 4090's 82 TFLOPS on ResNet.\n\nIn practical training scenarios, for 20B LLM fine-tuning, RTX 4090 takes 2-3 hours; H100 handles 70B in under one.\n\n## Inference Performance\n\nFor large language model inference, H100 hits 90.98 tokens/second on vLLM for LLMs; RTX 4090 reaches ~45 tokens/s. Image generation sees H100 at 36-49 images/minute versus RTX 4090's solid baseline.\n\n## Gaming and Creative Workloads\n\nWhen it comes to gaming and creative workloads, the RTX 4090 steels the show. Built on NVIDIA's Ada Lovelace architecture, it's designed to deliver stunning visuals and smooth performance in applications like Blender and Redshift.\n\n## Summary\n\nEach is optimized for different tasks; RTX 4090 excels in gaming and content creation, while H100 is for AI and computational tasks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"778ab94f-c220-445b-b967-5979274ad3a0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:13.203Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2d6609e-2e5e-42c9-8f89-d79808af1078","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bf6402f1-acf5-4872-8361-d1868fe4d24c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TScjPCWxzTuYoD4bCn47yM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PDLP first-order LP solver problem size threshold variables sparse small problems\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PDLP: A Practical First-Order Method for Large-Scale Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.07018v1\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLPx: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.14051\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Large Linear Programming Problems with NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-large-linear-programming-problems-with-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP+: A Further Enhanced GPU-Based First-Order Solver for Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.14051v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl: Experimental first-order solvers for linear and quadratic programming. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling up linear programming with PDLP\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/scaling-up-linear-programming-with-pdlp/\"},{\"title\":\"cuPDLP.jl: A GPU Implementation of Restarted Primal-Dual ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2311.12180\"},{\"title\":\"[2106.04756] Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.04756\"},{\"title\":\"An Overview of GPU-based First-Order Methods for Linear Programming and Extensions\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.02174\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - martinResearch/PySparseLP: python algorithms to solve sparse linear programming problems\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/martinResearch/PySparseLP\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about PDLP and its approach to problem sizes:\n\n## PDLP Overview\n\nPDLP is a practical first-order method for linear programming (LP) designed to solve large-scale LP problems. PDLP is based on the primal-dual hybrid gradient (PDHG) method applied to the minimax formulation of LP.\n\n## Key Design Features\n\nPDLP incorporates several enhancements to PDHG, including diagonal preconditioning, presolving, adaptive step sizes, adaptive restarting, and feasibility polishing. It can scale to very large problems because its core operation is matrix-vector multiplications.\n\n## Problem Size Capability\n\nRather than having a specific threshold that limits its application to small problems, PDLP is actually designed for the opposite: A new collection of eleven large-scale LP problems with sizes ranging from 125 million to 6.3 billion nonzeros was introduced to evaluate PDLP. This indicates that PDLP is built to handle very large sparse problems, not small ones.\n\nThe search results don't reveal any explicit threshold that would prevent PDLP from solving smaller problems—rather, the literature emphasizes its strengths on large-scale instances with billions of variables and constraints in sparse matrix form.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dd7f03cb-3fc0-4be7-b6cd-36c95b36cbd5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:14.171Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf6402f1-acf5-4872-8361-d1868fe4d24c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"92ab8cd8-7107-49e1-a6b6-6a89bccb9697","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149pFny1EX2TE2zZy35f4dk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"HiGHS 1.14 2026 release notes parallel performance LP\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"About · HiGHS Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/stable/\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel · HiGHS Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/dev/parallel/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ERGO-Code/HiGHS: Linear optimization software · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS optimization solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HiGHS_optimization_solver\"},{\"title\":\"highspy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/highspy/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · ERGO-Code/HiGHS\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS/releases\"},{\"title\":\"highspy - conda-forge | Anaconda.org\",\"url\":\"https://anaconda.org/conda-forge/highspy\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS Changelog — AMPL Resources\",\"url\":\"https://dev.ampl.com/solvers/highs/changes.html\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_HIGHS.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding HiGHS 1.14 and its features related to parallel performance for LP solving:\n\n## HiGHS 1.14 Release Highlights\n\nThe highlight of v1.14 is the extension of the HiPO interior point LP solver to handle convex QPs.\n\n## Parallel Performance and LP Solving\n\nRegarding parallel capabilities in HiGHS for LP problems:\n\nParallel computing for LP is currently restricted to the dual simplex solver for LP and the factorisation-based interior point solver. By default, the HiGHS dual simplex solver runs in serial, but it has a variant allowing concurrent processing that is used when the parallel option is set \"on\".\n\nThe interior point solver HiPO uses multiple threads to process the elimination tree during the multifrontal factorisation and to perform the dense factorisation of the frontal matrices, with the level of parallelism determined by the hipo_parallel_type option.\n\n## Future Developments\n\nNotably, a prototype multithreaded solver was completed in February 2026 and is expected to be released by June, with multi-threading within HiPO to be extended to other phases of the solver.\n\nThe search results don't contain a detailed comprehensive release notes document specifically listing all changes in version 1.14, but they do confirm version 1.14 exists and highlight its main improvements related to QP solving capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e89a9946-b97e-4b83-85ff-62a03cbb0842","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:14.387Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"92ab8cd8-7107-49e1-a6b6-6a89bccb9697","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b20d4a0f-5703-44bb-882e-291e9bbbea91","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a241150d7be611784","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbATBucmoh2pL9Gtbvxo1B","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cuOpt OR-Tools integration PuLP LP solver swap 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"pulp.apis Interface to Solvers — PuLP 4.0.0a6 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://coin-or.github.io/pulp/technical/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Decision Optimization Using Open Source NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-decision-optimization-using-open-source-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"cuOpt | Decision Optimization | NVIDIA\",\"url\":\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Support NVIDIA cuOpt solver · Issue #3626 · Pyomo/pyomo\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Pyomo/pyomo/issues/3626\"},{\"title\":\"PuLP · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/PuLP/\"},{\"title\":\"pulp.solvers Interface to Solvers — PuLP v1.4.6 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.coin-or.org/PuLP/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Projects – COIN-OR: Computational Infrastructure for Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.coin-or.org/projects/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - coin-or/pulp: A python Linear Programming API · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/pulp\"},{\"title\":\"Solvers in PuLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.educative.io/courses/master-linear-programming-python-pulp/solvers-in-pulp\"},{\"title\":\"How to add a new solver to PuLP — PuLP 3.3.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://coin-or.github.io/pulp/develop/add_solver.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cuOpt, OR-Tools integration, PuLP, and LP solver capabilities:\n\n## cuOpt and PuLP Integration\n\ncuOpt can be easily integrated into existing models built with PuLP and AMPL with minimal refactoring. cuOpt is available via third-party integration with AMPL, CVXPY, PuLP, GAMSPy, and JuMP.\n\n## cuOpt Capabilities\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt brings GPU acceleration to decision optimization, delivering massive speedups for real-world linear programming (LP), mixed-integer programming (MIP), and vehicle routing problems (VRP) workloads. cuOpt solves LP, MIP, and VRP problems 10x to 5,000x faster with GPU acceleration and is available as open source under the Apache 2.0 license.\n\n## COIN-OR Collaboration\n\nThis follows the recent announcement of the collaboration between COIN-OR and NVIDIA, further strengthening the ecosystem for optimization developers. As part of COIN-OR, cuOpt can be more easily discovered, extended, and used alongside other open source solvers.\n\n## Solver Options in PuLP\n\nPuLP can generate MPS or LP files and call solvers such as GLPK, COIN-OR CLP/CBC, CPLEX, GUROBI, MOSEK, XPRESS, CHOCO, MIPCL, HiGHS, SCIP/FSCIP.\n\nThe search results show robust support for integrating cuOpt with PuLP, though I didn't find specific information about \"OR-Tools integration\" or \"LP solver swap\" details in the 2026 timeframe in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"01f439b3-566a-4055-9987-ddeed369d41f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:21.201Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b20d4a0f-5703-44bb-882e-291e9bbbea91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
